          "note": "Read complete additional AHL physical pages 14–15 and individually displayed the matching image. Proposition 2.8 is explicitly conditional on the standard conjectures for all smooth projective varieties; it is not unconditional Hodge theory for arbitrary numerical Chow rings. Lemma 2.9 allows products of classes in the closure of K_A and invokes iterative boundary descent. Proposition 2.10 requires a graded subring B with one-dimensional top degree, no higher terms, nondegenerate multiplication pairing, and generation by classes in the closure of K_A; K_B is the relative interior of B^1 intersected with that closure, with a unique orientation sign. The overbars are verified in the image despite their loss in text extraction. Read the quotient-reduction part of the proof; the induction continues on the next selected page."
