          "reading_mode": "fresh_complete_selected_text_and_matching_image",
          "note": "Read complete Cattani physical pages 3–4 and individually displayed the matching image. Definition 2.3 specifies a finite-dimensional real graded module, nondegenerate parity-(−1)^k form S, commuting infinitesimal skew operators of degree −2, a compatible bigrading, a Lefschetz N_0, and primitive polarization. Its polarizing cone consists of compatible Lefschetz operators. For a degree-d real diagonal Hodge algebra one translates degree j to V_(d−2j), diagonal bidegree (d−j,d−j), and S(v_j,w_(d−j))=(−1)^j deg(v_j*w); this reconciles the skew/parity conventions with the usual commutative Hodge pairing. Page 3 explicitly warns that the descent proof is deep and uses variation of Hodge structure; it is not proved merely by finite linear algebra in this note."
