          "note": "Read complete Cattani physical pages 5–6 and individually displayed the matching image. Checked the weight/Hodge filtrations and the geometric regrading V_l=H^(k−l), V^(p,q)=H^(k−q,k−p). The simple-polytope apolar model uses all facet coordinates on the fixed-normal-fan virtual-polytope space and a strictly convex polarizing cone; it is not a theorem that an arbitrary smaller apolar algebra from a nef divisor substitution inherits all Hodge–Riemann relations. Timorin/Karu results in these examples remain cited foundations. Section 3's PVHS definitions start here; the exact descent statement remains to be read."
