          "note": "Read complete Cattani physical pages 7–8 and individually displayed the matching image. Read the PVHS/period-map setup and Theorem 3.1's proof outline with explicit Schmid/CKS splitting inputs. Theorem 3.2 states the precise descent condition: T+lambda*N_0 is Lefschetz for every lambda>0; image T*V is regraded by tilde V_l=T*V_(l+1), pairing tilde Q(Tu,Tv)=Q(u,Tv), weight drops by one. A multiplication operator for gamma in the closure of an open convex Hodge cone satisfies the condition because gamma+lambda*eta remains interior. Identifying the image with M/ann(gamma) and retaining the regraded pairing gives exactly AHL Lemma 4.6. This is a hypothesis/normalization check, not an independently reproved CKS descent lemma."
